# AI Notes – Ticket-to-FAQ Pipeline

## Project Title

AI-Powered Ticket-to-FAQ Pipeline

## Objective

The objective of this project is to automatically analyze closed customer support tickets, identify recurring issues, cluster similar tickets together, and generate FAQ drafts using Generative AI. This reduces manual effort in knowledge base creation and improves customer support efficiency.

## Problem Statement

Organizations receive a large number of support tickets daily. Many tickets describe similar issues, leading to repetitive work for support teams. Creating FAQs manually from these tickets is time-consuming and inefficient.

## Proposed Solution

The system collects closed support tickets from a CSV dataset, groups similar issues into clusters, and uses Google's Gemini AI to generate FAQ drafts. Administrators can review, approve, edit, and publish FAQs for future use.

## Technologies Used

* Python
* Streamlit
* SQLite
* Pandas
* Scikit-learn
* Google Gemini API
* GitHub

## System Workflow

1. Load closed ticket dataset.
2. Preprocess ticket descriptions.
3. Cluster similar tickets using machine learning.
4. Generate FAQ drafts using Gemini AI.
5. Admin reviews generated FAQs.
6. Approved FAQs are published.
7. Published FAQs become part of the knowledge base.

## Features

### Dashboard

Displays:

* Total Tickets
* Closed Tickets
* Clusters
* FAQ Drafts
* Published FAQs

### Closed Tickets

View all closed support tickets and their resolutions.

### Clusters

Groups similar support issues into categories.

### FAQ Draft Generation

Automatically creates FAQs from ticket clusters using Gemini AI.

### Admin Review

Allows approval, rejection, or modification of generated FAQs.

### Published FAQs

Stores approved FAQs and supports export functionality.

### Customer Portal

Simulates customer ticket submission.

### Support Panel

Simulates support staff resolving and closing tickets.

